<title>USA: Ten Oklahoma taxpayers sue firm on &quot;yield burning&quot;.</title>
<headline>Ten Oklahoma taxpayers sue firm on &quot;yield burning&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ten Oklahoma taxpayers have charged in state court that bond dealer Stifel, Nicolaus &amp; Co. allegedly made &quot;secret profits&quot; on a $109.8 million 1994 water resources deal and that a state board neglected to take proper action.</p>
<p>The December 17 lawsuit filed by Oklahoma lawyers Terry Guy Shipley and Charles Nesbitt for the 10 taxpayers appears to be the second action filed to date by a state or local government against bond dealers over a controversial bond market practice dubbed &quot;yield burning.&quot;</p>
</text>
